# grbl_ch32v006.elf.dump - `riscv64-unknown-elf-objdump -d -S -h -t --no-show-raw-insn <elf>` on the committed RELEASE
# .elf. Full disassembly + section headers + symbol table, plain
# text: when a size ratchet fires, `git diff` on THIS file shows the
# actual instruction-level change behind a byte-count drift, one
# level deeper than `.syms` (see artifacts/README.md).
#
# Flags, each picked for diff readability over completeness:
#   -d  disassemble CODE sections only - not -D/--disassemble-all,
#       which also decodes .data/.rodata/.debug bytes as bogus
#       instructions and would drown the real disassembly in noise
#   -S  intermix source where DWARF line info exists. RELEASE is
#       -g0 on every port (see each Makefile), so this is a verified
#       byte-for-byte no-op today (checked: identical output
#       with/without -S on a RELEASE build) - kept at zero cost so a
#       future -g-enabled RELEASE flavor gets source interleave for
#       free, without anyone remembering to add the flag then
#   -h  section headers (sizes/addresses/flags)
#   -t  full symbol table
#   --no-show-raw-insn  drop the raw hex encoding column (measured
#       ~24% smaller on stm32f103 RELEASE: 455508 -> 345950 bytes)
#       so the diff reads as instructions, not encoded bytes
#   (deliberately NOT -r: relocation entries are empty for a final
#    linked executable - verified empty on this build - so the flag
#    would only add a header for zero content; NOT --no-addresses:
#    unsupported by avr-objdump 2.26 and xc-dsc-objdump 2.32, so
#    using it would break two of the four toolchains this covers)
# Regenerate: `python3 tools/build_artifacts.py build --platforms ch32v006`.
#
# NOT HASH-GATED (`tools/build_artifacts.py check` verifies this
# file is PRESENT but does not compare its content - see do_check()
# and artifacts/README.md "elf.dump is not hash-gated"): objdump
# prints the exact path it was invoked with as the FIRST line of its
# own output, on every toolchain, regardless of any compiler flag -
# so this file is only byte-identical to a fresh rebuild when
# regenerated from the IDENTICAL absolute checkout path. Verified
# this batch: two RELEASE rebuilds of stm32f103 from different
# paths produced a BYTE-IDENTICAL .elf (cmp: no difference) but a
# 1-line-different .elf.dump (only the echoed path differed). This
# project's actual workflow (a fresh worktree per task) hits that
# path difference on effectively every `check` run, so hash-gating
# this file would false-positive constantly for zero real drift -
# the same CLASS of problem `-ffile-prefix-map` (see Makefiles)
# fixes for DEBUG .elf hashes, just not fixable the same way here
# since it's objdump's own invocation line, not an embedded DWARF
# attribute the compiler controls.

